implementations.guidance:
Selected GPIO output after mx_system_init: use resource port_symbol, pin_symbol and clock_enable_api (zero arguments; void). PA5 is a baseline output to adopt; PA4 needs initialization. Enable the selected clock, zero hal_gpio_config_t, set mode=HAL_GPIO_MODE_OUTPUT, output_type=HAL_GPIO_OUTPUT_PUSHPULL, pull=HAL_GPIO_PULL_NO, speed=HAL_GPIO_SPEED_FREQ_LOW, and explicitly set init_state=HAL_GPIO_PIN_SET (high) or HAL_GPIO_PIN_RESET (low) to the required safe level. Check HAL_GPIO_Init status. Init writes init_state before output mode; a prior WritePin alone does not preserve the intended level. Application owns polarity/CS timing; keep CS inactive through setup until transaction start. PA5 conflicts with SPI1 SCK. Pin/package mapping is sourced; external loads/LED/VCP wiring and electrical suitability remain unverified. HAL/LL sources are already included. Declarations below are provided by stm32_hal.h when USE_HAL_GPIO_MODULE==1; do not redeclare:
typedef struct
{
hal_gpio_mode_t mode;
hal_gpio_pull_t pull;
hal_gpio_speed_freq_t speed;
hal_gpio_output_t output_type;
hal_gpio_af_t alternate;
hal_gpio_pin_state_t init_state;
} hal_gpio_config_t;
hal_status_t  HAL_GPIO_Init(hal_gpio_t gpiox, uint32_t pins, const hal_gpio_config_t *p_config);
void HAL_GPIO_WritePin(hal_gpio_t gpiox, uint32_t pins, hal_gpio_pin_state_t pin_state);
void HAL_GPIO_TogglePin(hal_gpio_t gpiox, uint32_t pins);

